index 41ef141..07998d1 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -7,3 +7,18 @@ A tiny dependency-free Node HTTP service used to exercise the gated pipeline.
 - `src/users.js` is a local in-memory fake user store: synthetic users (`alice`, `bob`) whose
   salted scrypt hashes are computed at startup from synthetic passwords in `test/fixtures/users.js`.
 - Tests: `npm test` (`node --test "test/**/*.test.js"`).
+
+## POST /login
+
+`POST /login` with a JSON body `{"username": "...", "password": "..."}` (at most 4096 bytes):
+
+- `200 {"token": "..."}`: correct credentials; the token is 32 random bytes in base64url.
+- `401 {"error": "invalid credentials"}`: wrong password or unknown user (same body for both).
+- `429 {"error": "too many attempts"}` with `Retry-After`: 5 failed attempts for that username
+  within the last 60 seconds (sliding window; attempts still being verified count too).
+- `503` with `Retry-After: 1` and the 401 body: 4 password verifications are already running and
+  16 more are waiting on this server; not counted as a failed attempt.
+- `400 {"error": "invalid request"}` for a malformed body, `413 {"error": "payload too large"}`
+  for a body over 4096 bytes.
+
+Passwords and tokens are never logged. Sessions live in memory only (at most 10000).
